Build succeeds. Here's what was created:

**3 files added:**

1. **`Components/ScreenSize.cs`** — Enum with `Mobile`, `Tablet`, `Desktop` values.

2. **`Components/ScreenSizeProvider.razor`** — Wraps `ChildContent` in a `<CascadingValue>` of type `ScreenSize`. Uses JS interop to detect viewport width and listen for resize events. Defaults to `Desktop`.

3. **`Components/ScreenSizeProvider.razor.js`** — Collocated JS module that calls back into .NET when the viewport crosses the 768px/1024px breakpoints.

**Usage in child components:**

```razor
@code {
    [CascadingParameter]
    public ScreenSize ScreenSize { get; set; }
}
```

The component requires interactive Server rendering (already configured in your app) since it relies on JS interop.
